.SH NAME
.PP
auto-hyperthreading-toggle - Enable or disable Intel hyperthreading

\" Convention:
\" Underline anything that is typed verbatim - commands, etc.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
.nf 
.na
auto-hyperthreading-toggle state
.ad
.fi

.SH ARGUMENTS
.nf
.na
state   "on" or "off"
.ad
.fi

.SH DESCRIPTION

The
.B auto-hyperthreading-toggle
command enables or disables hyperthreading (Intel's brand of
SMT (simultaneous multithreading), using a boot-time variable
set in /boot/loader.conf.  A reboot is required to make the
change take effect.

.SH RETURN VALUES

0 on success, non-zero error codes otherwise.

.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
.na
auto-hyperthreading-toggle
.ad
.fi

